## Plan-text deviations (declared)

1. **Pyth org is `pyth-network` (lowercase) — not `PythNetwork`.** The plan
   body and Context7 reference both use the lowercase form, but the
   install instruction in the same plan body spells it `PythNetwork`
   (PascalCase). Used the working URL.

2. **Chainlink Solidity contracts are in `smartcontractkit/chainlink-evm` —
   not `smartcontractkit/chainlink`.** The legacy monorepo
   `smartcontractkit/chainlink` was split; Solidity moved to
   `chainlink-evm`. The `@chainlink/contracts` npm package is published
   from `chainlink-evm/contracts/`. Used `chainlink-evm` and let
   `chainlink-evm/=lib/chainlink-evm/contracts/` remapping apply.

3. **`forge init` in this foundry version uses `--no-git` (not
   `--no-commit`).** forge 1.4.4 made commit opt-in (`--commit`); the
   plan's `--no-commit` is the default in 1.4.4. Omitted both flags.

4. **`forge install` in this foundry version uses `--commit` (not
   `--no-commit`).** Same inversion as #3; the plan's `--no-commit` is
   the default. Omitted `--commit`.

5. **Deprecated `pyth-sdk-solidity` repo patched at install time.**
   Solc 0.8.24 rejects the deprecated Pyth files' backticked
   `@pythnetwork/...` doc tags with error 6546
   ("Documentation tag not valid for contracts"). Patched the 4 affected
   lines in 4 files with `sed` to drop the leading `@` inside the
   backticks. The semantic content of the comments is unchanged.
   This is the post-install patch the maintainer-suggested migration
   guide calls for; once the maintained package is wired in via
   `pyth-network/pyth-crosschain` the patch goes away. Documented
   in the Setup test header and in learnings.md.

6. **MockV3Aggregator constructor signature changed.** The current
   `chainlink-evm` takes `(uint8 decimals, int256 initialAnswer)` —
   not `(uint8, string description)`. The original (description-string)
   signature is preserved in `MockV3Aggregator.sol` only as a comment
   in some branches. Updated the Setup test to match.
